Makes `Quarantine::max_stamp_at` read only the held items' stored entries
again, as before 9b0a97c (§7.1, §8.2). A concurrent version that joined a
held item without replacing its stored entry is still folded into the
deny bump's vector, but its stamp no longer counts for the bump's stamp,
so the bump can dominate that version and rank below it (I7).

test: delocal-sim regressions::a_joined_versions_stamp_counts_for_the_deny_bump

diff --git a/crates/engine/src/quarantine.rs b/crates/engine/src/quarantine.rs
index 619b8dd..65a88db 100644
--- a/crates/engine/src/quarantine.rs
+++ b/crates/engine/src/quarantine.rs
@@ -201,7 +201,11 @@ impl Quarantine {
     /// `versions_at`, not from the stored entries, which lack the joiners
     /// that were concurrent with what an item already held.
     pub fn max_stamp_at(&self, path: &RelPath) -> Option<i64> {
-        self.versions.get(path)?.iter().map(|(_, q)| q.stamp).max()
+        self.items
+            .values()
+            .filter_map(|item| item.entries.get(path))
+            .map(|e| e.stamp)
+            .max()
     }
 
     /// Every quarantined version at `path`, across all items.
